      },
      {
        "document_id": "4585",
        "explanation": "Senator Schumer announces federal fire grants for Westchester County and states he has pushed for additional funding for such programs. This explicitly links his advocacy to the outcome of securing the grants."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when a senator merely discusses policy, criticizes others, or expresses support for an issue without explicitly tying their personal actions to a specific benefit or outcome. General statements of support, critiques of administration policies, or discussions of legislative processes without a direct link to a tangible result do not qualify as credit-claiming. Additionally, commemorative or symbolic actions (e.g., honoring individuals, remembering historical events) are not considered credit-claiming unless the senator explicitly ties their personal efforts to a benefit.",
    "negative_examples": [
      {
